From: Matthew Dowell <mbd06b+github@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 10:12:10 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 13/16] fix: restore the shared repository selector; rev-parse
 answers in .git alone

Re-review FIX FIRST item 1. `discovery_start()` (c4dd0d621) changed where
discovery starts for every command: from `/outer/sub/.git`, a directory
that is itself the top of a worktree with its own `.git`, the absolute
start skipped the child `.git`, ascended and selected `/outer`, so a
mutating command such as `branch create` would have written to the
enclosing repository. The helper is removed and the selector line is the
one at 7786c8185 again: `let repository = args.repository;`.

The `.git`-directory case is now answered inside the rev-parse spelling
only, after discovery has already failed: `outside_work_tree()` gives
Git's "must be run in a work tree" and 128 for a `--show-toplevel`
reached before any query that needs the repository. `--git-dir` or a
revision from inside `.git` itself fails at discovery again (status 1),
recorded as a known difference; below it (`.git/refs`) they work.

Journey: `a_worktree_named_dot_git_inside_another_repository_is_selected_like_git`
compares `rev-parse HEAD`, the path queries and `for-each-ref` with Git
from `/outer/sub/.git`; it fails on e534083f0's binary (outer HEAD) and
passes now.

